+### Client deployment policy
+
+The browser entry accepts `disabledActions` (empty by default) and `allowPromptWhileRunning` (true by default). An embedding supplies these through the public boot entry `config`; omitted config preserves standard behavior and changes require a page reload. Disabled create, fork, rename, prompt and queue operations fail locally before Remote calls. Busy refusal applies to prompt queue/steer and queued-message steering while the Session observes Host running state; queue removal and cancellation remain available unless separately disabled. These checks never grant resource permissions or replace Host admission.
