 <a id="understand-the-implementation"></a>
 ## Understand the implementation
 
+### Boot configuration
+
+Each public `WebBootEntry` may carry a JSON-object `config` passed to the browser plugin through the Cordis Loader. Omission uses plugin defaults; Host plugin configuration is not forwarded implicitly. Config survives code replacement. A different configuration for an existing entry rejects synchronization with `configuration changed; reload required`; the page must reload to adopt a new deployment policy. Graph `inject` edges ensure module factory arrival, not service activation order. Required services use Cordis injection.
+
