 The package injects the Client `remoteAccess` service and provides the root standard Hook `useWorkspaceAccess(workspaceId, action)`, which answers whether the current Peer may call `action` on one Workspace resource, and `ctx.uiWorkspace.whenAccess(workspaceId, action, callback)`, which keeps the callback's effects installed while that answer is true, with the semantics of `ctx.remoteAccess.whenAccess`; snapshot semantics belong to [`dsh-api-remote-access`](../../api/remote-access/README.md#client-face).
 
 <a id="understand-the-implementation"></a>
+### External navigation
+
+Client Config `navigationMode` defaults to `automatic`. In `external` mode this plugin activates only while the public `workspaceNavigation` service is available. Its `request()` receives distinct restore, Workspace-selection and New intents. The navigation owner validates saved identity hints, owns errors and explicit creation, and checks the request signal before opening or preparing drafts. Newer navigation or disposal aborts that signal; explicit navigation before catalog readiness supersedes startup restoration. No provider means no automatic fallback. `openWorkspace()` resolves after dispatch, not after provider completion; `connectWorkspace()` rejects. Explicit `ctx.sessions.create()` and `uiWorkspace.openSession()` remain separate operations. A Workspace is neither directory authorization nor native Session registration.
+
+Session deployment policy filters built-in menus, row actions and shortcuts, and guards rename requests and archive/pin execution. Remote owner status stays unchanged; plugins calling Remote directly still need Host enforcement.
+
+
